Article 1: Where a person commits the act specified in Article 338 of the Criminal Law, and any of the following circumstances exists, it shall be deemed as "seriously polluting the environment":
(1) discharging, dumping, or disposing of radioactive waste, waste containing pathogens of infectious diseases, or toxic substances in key protected areas determined according to law, such as drinking water source protection areas and core protection areas of protected natural areas;
(2) illegally discharging, dumping, or disposing of hazardous waste of three tons or more;
(3) discharging, dumping, or disposing of pollutants containing lead, mercury, cadmium, chromium, arsenic, thallium, or antimony, exceeding the national or local pollutant discharge standards by three times or more;
(4) discharging, dumping, or disposing of pollutants containing nickel, copper, zinc, silver, vanadium, manganese, or cobalt, exceeding the national or local pollutant discharge standards by ten times or more;
(5) discharging, dumping, or disposing of radioactive waste, waste containing pathogens of infectious diseases, or toxic substances through methods that evade supervision, such as underground pipes, seepage wells, seepage pits, fissures, karst caves, injection, or opening atmospheric emergency discharge channels under non-emergency circumstances;
(6) within two years, having been subjected to administrative punishment on two or more occasions for, during a heavy pollution weather warning period, violating state provisions and excessively discharging atmospheric pollutants subject to total emission control, such as sulfur dioxide and nitrogen oxides, and again committing such an act;
(7) a key pollutant-discharging unit or a unit under key management of pollutant discharge permits falsifying or forging automatic monitoring data or interfering with automatic monitoring facilities, and discharging pollutants such as chemical oxygen demand, ammonia nitrogen, sulfur dioxide, and nitrogen oxides;
(8) within two years, having been subjected to administrative punishment on two or more occasions for, in violation of state provisions, discharging, dumping, or disposing of radioactive waste, waste containing pathogens of infectious diseases, or toxic substances, and again committing such an act;
(9) illegal gains or causing losses of public or private property of 300,000 yuan or more;
(10) causing the interruption of water intake from township centralized drinking water sources for twelve hours or more;
(11) other circumstances of serious environmental pollution.

Article 2: Where a person commits the act specified in Article 338 of the Criminal Law, and any of the following circumstances exists, it shall be deemed as "serious circumstances":
(1) discharging, dumping, or disposing of radioactive waste, waste containing pathogens of infectious diseases, or toxic substances in key protected areas determined according to law, such as drinking water source protection areas and core protection areas of protected natural areas, causing degradation of ecological functions or serious damage to wildlife resources in the relevant areas;
(2) discharging, dumping, or disposing of radioactive waste, waste containing pathogens of infectious diseases, or toxic substances into the waters of important rivers or lakes determined by the state, causing degradation of ecological functions or serious damage to aquatic biological resources in the relevant waters;
(3) illegally discharging, dumping, or disposing of hazardous waste of one hundred tons or more;
(4) illegal gains or causing losses of public or private property of one million yuan or more;
(5) causing the interruption of water intake from centralized drinking water sources in county-level urban areas for twelve hours or more;
(6) causing the loss of basic functions or permanent damage to ten mu or more of permanent basic farmland or public welfare forest land, twenty mu or more of other agricultural land, or fifty mu or more of other land;
(7) causing the death of fifty cubic meters or more of forest or other trees, or the death of 2,500 or more saplings;
(8) causing the evacuation or relocation of 5,000 or more people;
(9) causing poisoning of thirty or more persons;
(10) causing serious injury or serious illness to one or more persons, or minor injury to three or more persons;
(11) other circumstances of a serious nature.

Article 3: Where a person commits the act specified in Article 338 of the Criminal Law, and any of the following circumstances exists, he or she shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than seven years and shall also be fined:
(1) discharging, dumping, or disposing of radioactive waste, waste containing pathogens of infectious diseases, or toxic substances in key protected areas determined according to law, such as drinking water source protection areas and core protection areas of protected natural areas, under any of the following circumstances:
1. causing the interruption of water intake from centralized drinking water sources in urban areas of a city divided into districts for twelve hours or more;
2. causing serious degradation of the ecosystem primarily protected in a protected natural area, or damage to the primarily protected natural landscapes;
3. causing serious damage to wildlife and plant resources under key national protection, or to the habitats or growing environments of species under key national protection;
4. other circumstances of a particularly serious nature.
(2) discharging, dumping, or disposing of radioactive waste, waste containing pathogens of infectious diseases, or toxic substances into the waters of important rivers or lakes determined by the state, under any of the following circumstances:
1. causing serious degradation of the ecosystem of the waters of important rivers or lakes determined by the state;
2. causing serious damage to wildlife and plant resources under key national protection;
3. other circumstances of a particularly serious nature.
(3) causing the loss of basic functions or permanent damage to fifty mu or more of permanent basic farmland;
(4) causing serious injury or serious illness to three or more persons, or serious disability or death to one or more persons.

Article 4: Where a person commits the act specified in paragraph 1 of Article 339 of the Criminal Law, and any of the following circumstances exists, it shall be deemed as "causing major losses to public or private property or seriously endangering human health":
(1) causing losses of public or private property of one million yuan or more;
(2) where any of the circumstances provided in items (5) to (10) of Article 2 of this Interpretation exists;
(3) other circumstances causing major losses to public or private property or seriously endangering human health.

Article 5: Where a person commits the criminal act specified in Article 338 or Article 339 of the Criminal Law, and any of the following circumstances exists, the person shall be given a heavier punishment:
(1) obstructing environmental supervision and inspection or investigation of an environmental emergency, where the act does not yet constitute a crime such as obstructing official duties;
(2) in or near densely populated areas such as hospitals, schools, and residential areas, violating state provisions by discharging, dumping, or disposing of radioactive waste, waste containing pathogens of infectious diseases, toxic substances, or other harmful substances;
(3) during the period of handling an environmental emergency or during a period of ordered rectification within a time limit, violating state provisions by discharging, dumping, or disposing of radioactive waste, waste containing pathogens of infectious diseases, toxic substances, or other harmful substances;
(4) an enterprise holding a hazardous waste business license, in violation of state provisions, discharging, dumping, or disposing of radioactive waste, waste containing pathogens of infectious diseases, toxic substances, or other harmful substances;
(5) an enterprise, public institution, or other producer or business operator under key management of pollutant discharge permits, without lawfully obtaining a pollutant discharge permit, discharging, dumping, or disposing of radioactive waste, waste containing pathogens of infectious diseases, toxic substances, or other harmful substances.

Article 10: Where personnel of an intermediary organization undertaking duties such as environmental impact assessment, environmental monitoring, inspection and testing of greenhouse gas emissions, or compilation or verification of emission reports intentionally provide false certification documents, and any of the following circumstances exists, the act shall be deemed as "serious circumstances" as provided in paragraph 1 of Article 229 of the Criminal Law:
(1) illegal gains of 300,000 yuan or more;
(2) within two years, having been subjected to administrative punishment on two or more occasions for providing false certification documents, and again providing false certification documents;
(3) other circumstances of a serious nature.
Where a person commits the act specified in the preceding paragraph, and provides false certification documents such as environmental impact assessment in major projects or programs involving public safety, causing particularly major losses to public property and the interests of the state and the people, the person shall, in accordance with paragraph 1 of Article 229 of the Criminal Law, be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than five years but not more than ten years, and shall also be fined.
Where a person commits the acts specified in the preceding two paragraphs and simultaneously extorts property from others or illegally accepts property from others, constituting a crime, the person shall be convicted and punished according to the provisions providing the heavier punishment.

Article 11: Where a person, in violation of state provisions, commits any of the following acts against an environmental quality monitoring system, or compels, instigates, or prompts another person to commit any of the following acts, and the consequences are serious, the person shall, in accordance with Article 286 of the Criminal Law, be convicted and punished for the crime of destroying computer information systems:
(1) modifying system parameters or monitoring data stored, processed, or transmitted in the system;
(2) interfering with system sampling, causing monitoring data to be seriously distorted because the system cannot operate normally;
(3) other acts of destroying an environmental quality monitoring system.
Where a key pollutant-discharging unit or a unit under key management of pollutant discharge permits falsifies or forges automatic monitoring data or interferes with automatic monitoring facilities, and discharges pollutants such as chemical oxygen demand, ammonia nitrogen, sulfur dioxide, and nitrogen oxides, and the act simultaneously constitutes the crime of environmental pollution and the crime of destroying computer information systems, the unit shall be convicted and punished according to the provisions providing the heavier punishment.
Where personnel engaged in the maintenance or operation of environmental monitoring facilities implement or participate in implementing acts such as falsifying or forging automatic monitoring data, interfering with automatic monitoring facilities, or destroying an environmental quality monitoring system, they shall be given a heavier punishment according to law.

Article 17: The following substances shall be deemed as "toxic substances" as specified in Article 338 of the Criminal Law:
(1) hazardous waste, meaning solid waste with hazardous characteristics that is listed in the National Catalogue of Hazardous Wastes or is identified according to the national standards and methods for identifying hazardous waste;
(2) substances listed in the annexes to the Stockholm Convention on Persistent Organic Pollutants;
(3) pollutants whose heavy metal content exceeds the national or local pollutant discharge standards;
(4) other substances that are toxic and may pollute the environment.
